> browser:click-entry: npm run test:click-entry-browser

> @openpresentation/opf-editor@0.18.1 test:click-entry-browser
> node test/click-entry-browser.mjs

Click entry: 18 browser workflows passed.
 - title: one click puts a collapsed caret at the clicked glyph half (left and right halves, start, middle, end)
 - wrapped subtitle: double spaces, tab, wrapped lines and clicks outside the glyphs map to exact source offsets
 - bullets: a wrapped list item maps line by line
 - centered and right-aligned titles
 - footer furniture text
 - CRLF source: LF input offsets, typing after a click keeps the original line endings
 - rich text: caret at the click, no select-all, double-click selects a word
 - press-drag selects a forward, backward and multi-line range without moving anything
 - while editing: double-click selects a word, triple-click a paragraph, clicks move the caret
 - clicking another text target commits then enters at the click; an invalid edit refuses
 - Enter, Space and F2 select all; Escape keeps the box selected
 - images and charts: click selects, double-click opens properties
 - layout handles still drag and text beside them still edits
 - textEntry "dblclick": click selects, double-click places the caret, Enter selects all
 - untraced text falls back to the positioned textarea layout
 - a secondary button does not enter editing
 - reveal shows the slide and selects the nearest target
 - touch: a tap enters at the tapped character

